Theorem VF-3: Layer 3 oracle re-derivation — re-derived MemoryContract refines the inferred contract

  Preconditions:
    - VF-3 governs the Layer-3 oracle verifier per Annex E §AIMS VF-3:
      "re-derives MemoryContract from realized IR + compares against inferred
      contract along access, consumption, effects. Unsafe mismatches (analysis
      more optimistic than realization) = errors."
    - VF-3's concrete shape is ArcFunction -> MemoryContract (the re-derived
      side of the contract) per aims-proof/proofs/01-verification/Verification.proof.
      Discharged here against the sec-01 Verification.proof sorry obligation.
    - Re-derivation is SUBJECT-INDEPENDENT. The realized-evidence carrier has
      only realizable CFG paths, realized terminal-use kinds, explicit local
      credits/releases, and semantic demand tokens. It contains no inferred
      ParamContract field. In particular, inferred iter_consumes and
      borrowed_cow_consumed cannot mint an opening credit.
    - Access starts each realized path at LOCAL funding zero. Explicit positive
      RcInc credit funds a later non-iter transfer/release. The committed
      ApplyToIterConsumingParam terminal-use kind is independently observed and
      represents caller-funded inward transfer; it does not consume local
      credit. Borrowed is sufficient iff every path remains prefix-nonnegative.
    - Consumption composes semantic demand with TF-11 seq_add within a path and
      IC-3 component join across alternative paths. Raw CFG visit counts and
      aggregate operation counts are not demand evidence.
    - Semantic demand identity follows SSA value provenance and exact CFG-edge
      alternatives. Value-producing definitions cut backward demand;
      transparent aliases and block-parameter flow preserve it on the exact
      incoming edge. Physical return/storage aliasing is a separate RC/share
      relation and cannot manufacture demand across a definition.
    - Realized endpoint normalization deduplicates only a structurally proven
      multi-instruction lowering of one source demand. A shared source span is
      corroboration, not identity: distinct same-span sites and generated or
      no-span sites remain distinct. Loop recurrence remains repeated demand.
    - The comparison is a REFINEMENT check along three dimensions (access,
      consumption, effects): the re-derived contract MUST be lattice-<= the
      inferred contract (the realized IR is no MORE demanding than the inferred
      contract claimed). An UNSAFE mismatch is the re-derived value EXCEEDING
      the inferred value (analysis was too optimistic — the realized IR needs
      more than the contract promised).
    - Compiler conformance site:
        * compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/verify/oracle.rs
          verify_coherence must extract the independent realized evidence above
          before comparing it with the inferred contract. Agreement between two
          contract-driven algorithms is not VF-3 evidence. General-effects
          coverage beyond the shipped subset remains target-only per Annex E.
    - depends-on sec-02: L-1..L-5 lattice properties are load-bearing for the
      re-derived contract being lattice-<= the inferred contract; L-6
      monotonicity is the cross-layer invariant VF-3 preserves.
    - depends-on sec-06: IC-3 ParamContract + IC-5 EffectSummary soundness is
      load-bearing for the re-derived contract dimensions.

  Soundness property:
    Forall realized ArcFunction F with inferred MemoryContract C_inferred and
    re-derived MemoryContract C_rederived = oracle(F):

      (P1) Refinement direction: F is SAFE iff C_rederived <= C_inferred on
           every compared dimension (access, consumption, effects). F is UNSAFE
           (an oracle error) iff C_rederived > C_inferred on any dimension —
           the realized IR demands more than the inferred contract promised,
           meaning the analysis was too optimistic.

      (P2) Per-dimension comparison: access, consumption, and effects are each
           compared independently in the lattice partial order. ANY single
           dimension where C_rederived > C_inferred is an unsafe mismatch; SAFE
           requires every dimension to refine.

      (P3) Independent Access evidence: each path starts at local count zero.
           A non-iter ownership transfer/release requires a preceding explicit
           realized credit. A later credit cannot self-fund an earlier transfer,
           and a funded branch cannot mask an unfunded alternative.

      (P4) Independent iter evidence: ApplyToIterConsumingParam is recognized
           from the committed realized terminal-use kind and compared with the
           inferred iter bit. The inferred bit cannot create evidence or credit.

      (P5) Demand composition: sequential semantic demands use TF-11 seq_add;
           alternative path demands use IC-3 join. Two alternative Linear uses
           remain Linear; two sequential Linear uses become Unrestricted. Two
           instructions assigned one proven semantic endpoint remain one
           Linear use, while distinct same-span/no-span endpoints remain
           Unrestricted when sequential.

    VF-3 is the oracle layer: it re-derives the contract from the realized side
    and checks the inferred side was not too optimistic. A contract that under-
    claims (re-derived <= inferred) is safe — the realized IR is within the
    promised envelope. A contract that over-claims (re-derived > inferred) is an
    error — downstream consumers acting on the optimistic inferred contract
    would be unsound.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the refinement engine via definitional rewriting
    of the lattice partial order (per the proof-checker design
    sec-Engine-per-Category-Inventory VF row; the foundational-axiom policy
    sec-Per-Engine-Constructive-Proof-Shape — definitional rewriting +
    structural congruence + constructive ->-introduction).

    Part (P1/P2) — per-dimension refinement grid:

      The verifier models the lattice rank on each compared dimension (access:
      Borrowed < Owned; consumption: Dead < Linear < Affine < Unrestricted;
      effects: false < true, OR-monotone) and asserts SAFE iff re_derived_rank
      <= inferred_rank on every dimension. Discharged rows:
        exact_match_safe — equal on every dimension -> SAFE.
        rederived_below_inferred_safe — re-derived <= inferred on all -> SAFE.
        access_too_optimistic_unsafe — re-derived Owned vs inferred Borrowed
                                        -> UNSAFE.
        consumption_too_optimistic_unsafe — re-derived Unrestricted vs inferred
                                        Linear -> UNSAFE.
        effect_too_optimistic_unsafe — re-derived may_allocate vs inferred pure
                                        -> UNSAFE.
      Coverage gate: 5 rows (2 safe + 3 unsafe, one unsafe per dimension).

    Negative-direction witness (the refinement direction has teeth — analysis-
    too-optimistic is REJECTED):
      A re-derived Owned access against an inferred Borrowed contract is flagged
      UNSAFE; accepting it would let realization demand more than the contract
      promised (a miscompilation where a caller treats the value as Borrowed but
      realization owns it).

    Realized-evidence discharge (compiled AimsProof.Oracle):
      RealizedParamEvent, RealizedParamPath, RealizedParamEvidence,
      RealizedParamEvent.localFundingEvents,
      RealizedParamPath.locallyFunded,
      RealizedParamEvidence.access,
      RealizedParamEvidence.iterTransfers,
      RealizedParamEvidence.iterTransferAgrees,
      RealizedParamEvidence.consumption,
      RealizedParamEvidence.contractDims,
      RealizedParamEvidence.oracleAccepts,
      VF3_independent_oracle_acceptance_iff,
      VF3_local_credit_funds_borrowed_transfer,
      VF3_inferred_self_funding_rejected,
      VF3_uncredited_borrowed_cow_release_requires_owned,
      VF3_iter_transfer_is_independent_inward_funding,
      VF3_inferred_iter_claim_cannot_create_evidence,
      VF3_branch_with_unfunded_transfer_requires_owned,
      VF3_consumption_sequential_matches_TF11,
      VF3_consumption_alternative_matches_IC3,
      VF3_duplicate_lowering_endpoint_is_linear,
      VF3_distinct_same_span_endpoints_are_unrestricted,
      VF3_generated_distinct_endpoints_are_unrestricted,
      VF3_endpoint_alternatives_remain_linear,
      VF3_alternative_single_uses_are_not_unrestricted,
      VF3_sequential_single_uses_are_unrestricted,
      VF3_local_credit_implies_may_share,
      VF3_borrowed_boundary_propagates_may_share,
      VF3_may_share_alternative_matches_IC3.

    Engines dispatched:
      refinement (PRIMARY — section_09::verify_vf3_oracle_rederivation;
        per-dimension lattice-<= refinement over the safe/unsafe grid; emits
        Fail on a safe/unsafe mismatch or a wrongly-accepted too-optimistic
        contract)
      structural_induction (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the
        coverage-manifest VF row)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      interprocedural_summary (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_09 refinement discharges the lattice comparison, while compiled AimsProof.Oracle discharges subject-independent realized evidence: zero-seeded per-path local funding, terminal-kind iter evidence, SSA/CFG endpoint identity, TF-11 sequential demand, IC-3 alternative demand, and negative witnesses for inferred self-funding, an unfunded branch, branch-count inflation, and same-span/no-span over-deduplication
